@startuml
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "User (Browser)" as User
participant "Frontend" as FE
box "Infrastructure" #f9f9f9
    participant "Nginx" as Nginx
    participant "API Gateway" as Auth
    database "Redis\n(Sessions)" as Redis
end box
participant "Collab Service\n(Socket.io)" as Collab

== Phase 1: Ticket Acquisition ==

User -> FE: Wants to join session
FE -> Nginx: POST /api/collab/join\nAuth: [Firebase Token]
Nginx -> Auth: Forward (strip /api)
activate Auth
Auth -> Auth: Validate Firebase Token\nCheck session membership
Auth -> Redis: SET ticket:UUID\n{uid, sessionId} EX 60
Auth --> FE: 200 OK { ticket: "UUID" }
deactivate Auth

== Phase 2: WebSocket Connection ==

FE -> Nginx: WS Upgrade Request\n/socket.io/?ticket=UUID
activate Nginx
Nginx -> Collab: Proxy Upgrade\n(plain passthrough, no auth_request)
activate Collab

Collab -> Collab: Socket.IO middleware:\nextract ticket from query

Collab -> Redis: GETDEL ticket:UUID
Redis --> Collab: {uid, sessionId} or null

alt Ticket Valid
    Collab -> Collab: Attach userId & sessionId\nto socket object
    Collab --> FE: HTTP 101 Switching Protocols
    FE <-> Collab: Authenticated WebSocket
else Ticket Invalid/Expired/Missing
    Collab --> FE: Connection rejected\n(Socket.IO error event)
end

deactivate Collab
deactivate Nginx

note over Collab, Redis
  Design note: Ticket validation is done in the
  collab service middleware, not via nginx auth_request.
  nginx auth_request interferes with WebSocket upgrades.
end note

@enduml